\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{Four Lie-group proposals remain open}
\date{2026-11-02}

\p{The four names #{Sp(3,1)}, #{SU(3,1)}, #{SU(3,2)} and
#{SL(4,\mathbb R)} remain open tests against
[the compatibility datum](fdip-009Z). No matrix realization,
coefficient field, dimension, representation, or action on a
finite graph is given for any of them in these notes. The
finite maps proved for [the binary tetrahedral spinor](fdip-00A0)
are not claimed to factor through these groups.}

\p{For each name, \ref{fdip-00A1} records the symbol as an
unconstructed comparison with a Dirac, Lorentz, gauge or
gravitational structure. The known algebraic datum is the
symbol itself. The missing map is a stated homomorphism,
kernel, cover or branching rule, together with a selector and
a reference object. No finite witness is supplied: no finite
subgroup, matrix model, or branching rule from #{2T} is
identified with any of the four names. All five criteria are
therefore open. The open mark does not assert that a later
realization is impossible.}
